{"name":"Serious Moonlight","hex":"#f9e0cd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"serious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without humor or expression of happiness; grave in manner or disposition.","Important; weighty; not insignificant."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["seriously, in a serious manner"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serious"},{"term":"moonlight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The light reflected from the Moon, which seems to emanate from it.","The silvery colour of the light reflected by the Moon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To do a moonlight flit: to secretly leave premises without paying the rent, supposedly at night by the light of the Moon.","To do a moonlight flit: to secretly leave premises without paying the rent, supposedly at night by the light of the Moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Let's Dance (David Bowie song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Let's Dance\" is a song by the English singer-songwriter David Bowie, originally included as the title track of his 1983 album of the same name. Co-produced by Nile Rodgers of Chic, it was recorded in late 1982 at the Power Station in New York City. With the assistance of engineer Bob Clearmountain, Rodgers transformed the song from its folk rock origins to a dance number through studio effects and new musicians Bowie had yet to work with. Bowie hired then-unknown Texas guitarist Stevie Ray Vaughan, who added a blues edge."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/41/LetsDance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let's_Dance_(David_Bowie_song)"},{"title":"Serious Moonlight (1983 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Serious Moonlight is a concert video by the English singer-songwriter David Bowie. Filmed in Vancouver on 12 September 1983, on the singer's \"Serious Moonlight Tour\", the video was released on VHS and laserdisc in 1984 and on DVD in 2006. The concert includes most of the songs from the concert although \"Star\", \"Stay\", \"The Jean Genie\", \"Red Sails\" and \"Modern Love\" were left off the 1984 release due to time constraints; the songs were not reinstated for the 2006 DVD release."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/BowieSeriousMoonlight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Moonlight_(1983_film)"},{"title":"Serious Moonlight (2009 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Serious Moonlight is a 2009 American black comedy film directed by Cheryl Hines and starring Meg Ryan, Timothy Hutton, Kristen Bell, and Justin Long. It was released by Magnolia Pictures on 4 December 2009."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Serious_moonlight_09_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Moonlight_(2009_film)"},{"title":"Moonlight","blocks":[{"text":"Moonlight is light from the surface of the Moon, consisting mostly of reflected sunlight, and some earthlight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Earthshine_Moon.jpg/330px-Earthshine_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonlight"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Nilerodgersatlecrib.jpg/500px-Nilerodgersatlecrib.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Nilerodgersatlecrib.jpg/500px-Nilerodgersatlecrib.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nile Rodgers (pictured in 1999) was instrumental in the arrangement and production of \"Let's Dance\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANilerodgersatlecrib.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Stevie_Ray_Vaughan_Live_1983.jpg/500px-Stevie_Ray_Vaughan_Live_1983.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Stevie_Ray_Vaughan_Live_1983.jpg/500px-Stevie_Ray_Vaughan_Live_1983.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blues guitarist Stevie Ray Vaughan (pictured in 1983) contributed guitar to the track.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStevie_Ray_Vaughan_Live_1983.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg/500px-Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg/1280px-Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg/500px-Carinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Carinda Hotel, the pub where scenes with the dancing couple were filmed.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarinda_Hotel_09-08-2024_002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/The_Breadknife.jpg/500px-The_Breadknife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/The_Breadknife.jpg/500px-The_Breadknife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Part of the music video was shot at the Breadknife in Warrumbungle National Park.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Breadknife.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Bowie_1983_s